                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is the literal \"mobile game moneygrab-VR-Port\" : It is one of those \"find the item\" casual games that can work quite well on a phone, and could, in theory work in an okay way in VR. \nFirst, what was modified for VR : the controls in Wrath of Loki have been adapted for tracked controllers, and the probably nice handdrawn images have been mapped as 360 panoramas.\nI say \"probably\" as the developer didn't use high res pictures and *everything* is pixely and completely fugly. It looks a mess. This is also the only art you will see. There is no use of 3D at all, except for the fact that you are standing in a textured dome. Everything is scaled badly (standard problem with flat panoramas in VR) and more reminiscent of a bad Jackson Pollock painting than modern graphics.\nif at least the picture were not a blurry mess of pixels and colour banding, but instead of pristine quality, I wouldn't complain too much. Would still be a low effort product, but at least it would be pleasing to the eye.\nEven better if, instead of just reusing the assets the developer had recreated the scenes in 3D.\n\nBut the way this was thrown together quickly without , all I can say is that it is REALLY not worth the price and disk space.\n",
